October's free PlayStation plus games  have been officially revealed and the  alleged GTA 6 hacker has appeared in  court cue the Law and Order music  PlayStation has announced the PS Plus  free games lineup for October 2022 and  remember all tiers of PlayStation Plus  subscribers will be able to claim these  starting on October 4th Hot Wheels  Unleashed is an arcade racing game that  was released last year to pretty solid  reviews and may or may not have caused  me to start collecting Hot Wheels again  in real life my wife hates it though  Unleashed can get a bit repetitive the  racing mechanics are solid and there are  a lot of tracks you can also build your  own tracks and then race online against  friends both the PS5 and PS4 versions of  Hot Wheels unleash will be available to  claim now if you haven't played  Injustice 2 then you're in for a treat  even though it's 5 years old at this  point Injustice 2 still looks and plays  great it features a ton of unique  content including a wonderfully made  story mode and a boatload of challenges  with unique rewards the expansive roster  is bolstered by a cool leveling and gear  system that rewards players who keep  playing the lineup is rounded out by  super hot one of the best Indie Games in  recent years super hot is a first person  shooter that plays like a puzzle game  your objective is to get through each  room without getting shot and it  features a very clever mechanic time  only moves when you move so each time  you stop enemies freeze too it's a  stylish and unique game that everyone  should try at least once make sure to  claim September's PS plus lineup before  October 4th because it includes a couple  of great games as well Switching gears  to GTA now and some legal drama London  Police have arrested a 17 year old  suspected of perpetrating the recent  hack on Rockstar Games which resulted in  the unprecedented leaking of  in-development Grand Theft Auto 6  footage as reported by Eurogamer the  suspect entered a non-guilty plea  related to computer misuse but did plead  guilty to violating bail conditions the  arrest made on September 22nd was  announced by the city of London Police  Twitter account the following day in its  initial post the police department did  not specify if the hacker described as a  17 year old from Oxfordshire was  suspected of hacking Rockstar Games  however it did say it was a part of an  investigation made in collaboration with  the UK's National cyber crime unit  Eurogamer later reported that the  suspect was believed to have been behind  the Rockstar attack as part of a larger  group called lapsis and it was not the  first time they had allegedly been on  the wrong side of the law it's unclear  what penalties the suspect could face or  what action take two may take against  them and now let's take a moment to give  Call of Duty and cyberpunk their flowers  despite its slightly convoluted schedule  the Modern Warfare 2 Beta saw the  largest turnout for any Call of Duty  beta including the number of players  hours played and number of matches  played on all platforms across the two  beta weekends players who progressed in  the beta will also be able to unlock  exclusive rewards when the full game is  released on October 28th meanwhile CD  projekt Red is celebrating 20 million  copies of cyberpunk 2077 sold so  congrats to them we'll all ignore the  number of refunds for today but today  only now let me know in the comments if  you bought cyberpunk recently if you  bought it in the past and then returned  it and then bought it again and then uh  pressure me to play it because I I own a  copy and I'm still maybe like 20 minutes  into it I'll see you tomorrow
 

